  "question": {
    "text": "Which substance has a dipole moment?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is similar to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> (tetrahedral) but it has three different bond angles.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HCCl</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ClCCl</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;which are close to but not equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>109</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Since, electronegativity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> the bond dipole moments do not cancel and the molecule has a dipole moment.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0022_2dac9e1fb4c4.png\" style=\"width: 199px; height: 209px;\" /></p>"
